WEBVTT

1
00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.040
Oh. that's beautiful.

2
00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:26.710
It was terrible. I can't do it.

3
00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:28.410
Hmm. not yet.

4
00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:31.040
But you will.

5
00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:38.390
You're growing up so fast.

6
00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:41.230
- You say that all the time.

7
00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:41.230
- Yeah. it's because you are.

8
00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:46.620
You look so much like your sister.

9
00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:53.800
I wish I could remember her.

10
00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:04.090
If I come back and you're a foot taller...

11
00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:06.710
gonna ground you.

12
00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:12.540
Shh.

13
00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.850
Remember what we learned. okay?

14
00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:39.230
Eve. come with me.

15
00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:44.940
Stay quiet.

16
00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:03.890
We opened our hearts to you.

17
00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.620
We embraced you.

18
00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:12.860
We let you. an outsider.

19
00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:12.860
marry a daughter of our clan.

20
00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:15.340
And how did you repay this kindness?

21
00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:19.970
You took what was not rightfully yours.

22
00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:26.510
And now. your wife is dead.

23
00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:26.510
to atone for your transgressions.

24
00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:30.420
Did you think that

25
00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:30.420
you could just walk away?

26
00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:32.150
Hmm?

27
00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:35.210
Where is she?

28
00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:37.150
Where is Eve?

29
00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:42.690
Charming.

30
00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:52.830
You're a fucking coward.

31
00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:57.600
You're trying to convince yourself

32
00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:57.600
that fate absolves you of your actions.

33
00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:00.180
There are no choices.

34
00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:02.770
Yeah. Does that make

35
00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:02.770
what you do any easier?

36
00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:05.040
It makes what I do...

37
00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:07.350
necessary.

38
00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:18.560
One bullet...

39
00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:20.960
well placed...

40
00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:25.400
can be a magical thing.

41
00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:27.900
It's neither good...

42
00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:30.040
nor evil.

43
00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:33.480
But how a man uses it

44
00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:36.210
reveals his true character.

45
00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:41.990
You wanted choices.

46
00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:44.460
Well. here they are.

47
00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:46.460
You kill yourself.

48
00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:48.660
and your daughter lives.

49
00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:51.760
Or kill me.

50
00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:54.770
and you and your daughter die together.

51
00:07:58.070 --> 00:07:59.840
Choice is yours.

52
00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:13.590
You've got your choice.

53
00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:16.620
Now. do you have the balls to do it?

54
00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:28.260
Papa!

55
00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:31.720
Hey. baby. look at me.

56
00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:33.270
- It's okay.

57
00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:39.010
Come on.

58
00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:08.960
Come on.

59
00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:46.260
Papa.

60
00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.170
I'm sorry. honey.

61
00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:53.010
- I never wanted this for you.

62
00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:53.010
- Papa.

63
00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.180
I'm sorry.

64
00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:00.610
Papa!

65
00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:02.480
Papa...

66
00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:08.880
Tchaikovsky. How lovely.

67
00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:21.660
At a time of loss.

68
00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:21.660
there's nothing easier than pity

69
00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:26.700
and nothing more difficult than the truth.

70
00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:26.700
as there are no easy answers for grief.

71
00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:29.710
I'd like to be honest with you.

72
00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:32.710
Would that be all right?

73
00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:50.060
Your father was a good man.

74
00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:56.730
He wanted a free and open life for you.

75
00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:01.980
Not like the one that he had to endure.

76
00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:07.250
But we all live

77
00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:07.250
with the decisions we make.

78
00:13:10.050 --> 00:13:12.040
Now he's been taken from you.

79
00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:14.820
I can do nothing about that.

80
00:13:16.660 --> 00:13:18.290
But what I can do...

81
00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:21.490
is offer to take you to his family.

82
00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:24.330
They will look after you

83
00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:27.590
and. hopefully...

84
00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:30.930
one day become your family. too.

85
00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:50.880
The Director will see you now.

86
00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:04.990
Does she know who her parents really were?

87
00:15:19.910 --> 00:15:21.280
Come here. Sit.

88
00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:28.250
You dance. yes?

89
00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:32.520
- Mm-hmm.

90
00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:32.520
- I run this theater.

91
00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:36.290
and I am always looking for new recruits.

92
00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:42.260
I know you.

93
00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:44.960
I know your pain.

94
00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:48.440
What boils inside of you

95
00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:48.440
under the surface.

96
00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:53.480
I can give you somewhere

97
00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:53.480
to put that anger.

98
00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:57.320
Those men took your past.

99
00:15:57.420 --> 00:15:59.480
Don't let them steal your future.

100
00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:15.300
Well?

101
00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:18.970
She says my path is now here

102
00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:18.970
with the Ruska Roma.

103
00:16:23.110 --> 00:16:24.310
Very well...

104
00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:26.440
Eve.

105
00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:31.310
Thank you. Mr. Winston.

106
00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:34.860
You are most welcome. Miss MaCarro.

107
00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:46.100
And know that I will

108
00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:46.100
always be at your service.

109
00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:05.150
My name is Nogi.

110
00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:07.120
Did you know my father?

111
00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:09.010
I did.

112
00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:17.190
Your father was Ruska Roma. like me.

113
00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:18.630
Like you will be. too.

114
00:17:22.070 --> 00:17:24.900
He was what we call Kikimora.

115
00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:26.410
What is that?

116
00:17:27.010 --> 00:17:28.870
In Slavic mythology.

117
00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:35.180
the Kikimora is a kind of spirit

118
00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:35.180
to those with darkness in their hearts.

119
00:17:35.250 --> 00:17:38.710
She can be vengeful and destructive.

120
00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:41.350
Like the boogeyman?

121
00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:44.520
Yes.

122
00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:47.760
But to the innocent...

123
00:17:47.860 --> 00:17:49.890
she can be a protector.

124
00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:57.230
It is...

125
00:17:58.940 --> 00:18:00.410
two sides...

126
00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:03.110
to the one coin.

127
00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:05.240
To kill...

128
00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:11.280
to save.

129
00:18:14.090 --> 00:18:17.290
But. ultimately...

130
00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:24.300
it is up to you to choose.

131
00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:30.830
Are you finished?

132
00:19:32.470 --> 00:19:33.930
No.

133
00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:35.490
Good.

134
00:19:36.370 --> 00:19:38.170
That will be all for today.

135
00:19:38.270 --> 00:19:42.370
Tend to your wounds before you get sepsis.

136
00:19:38.270 --> 00:19:42.370
and we have to cut off your feet.

137
00:19:43.010 --> 00:19:45.100
Tell Tatiana she's next.

138
00:20:14.910 --> 00:20:16.840
"Her Majesty" says you're up.

139
00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:19.540
That woman hates me.

140
00:20:21.020 --> 00:20:22.420
She hates everybody.

141
00:20:28.560 --> 00:20:30.080
Christ. Eve.

142
00:20:30.190 --> 00:20:32.220
Why do you push yourself like this?

143
00:20:33.760 --> 00:20:35.020
I want to be ready.

144
00:20:36.030 --> 00:20:37.020
Ready for what?

145
00:20:40.740 --> 00:20:42.070
You know what's funny?

146
00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:45.110
When I was a little girl. I actually

147
00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:45.110
did want to be a real ballerina.

148
00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:47.230
You are a real ballerina.

149
00:20:48.340 --> 00:20:49.940
You're the best dancer here.

150
00:20:51.010 --> 00:20:52.840
That other shit.

151
00:20:51.010 --> 00:20:52.840
you'll learn with training.

152
00:21:13.100 --> 00:21:14.260
Fire!

153
00:21:17.300 --> 00:21:18.900
One bullet.

154
00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:22.430
well placed. can change the world.

155
00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:32.910
The Kikimora's purpose is

156
00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:32.910
to stop that bullet.

157
00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:41.920
Time's up!

158
00:21:47.100 --> 00:21:52.560
To become Kikimora

159
00:21:47.100 --> 00:21:52.560
you must become the assassin.

160
00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:56.740
<i>You must learn to move like him</i>

161
00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:56.740
<i>and think like him.</i>

162
00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:01.780
For this next exercise.

163
00:22:01.850 --> 00:22:05.010
we will be using simulated rounds.

164
00:22:05.120 --> 00:22:06.420
What are the rules?

165
00:22:06.490 --> 00:22:10.120
Protect your ward at all costs.

166
00:22:11.130 --> 00:22:13.460
<i>That is the only rule.</i>

167
00:22:46.990 --> 00:22:48.830
Why did you fail?

168
00:22:48.900 --> 00:22:50.230
He's too strong.

169
00:22:50.330 --> 00:22:51.660
Do you really believe

170
00:22:51.730 --> 00:22:55.030
that strength has anything to do

171
00:22:51.730 --> 00:22:55.030
with whether you win or lose?

172
00:22:55.140 --> 00:22:57.370
You will always be weaker.

173
00:22:58.740 --> 00:23:01.640
You will always be smaller

174
00:22:58.740 --> 00:23:01.640
and at a disadvantage.

175
00:23:03.310 --> 00:23:04.570
He is beating you

176
00:23:04.680 --> 00:23:08.510
because you are allowing him

177
00:23:04.680 --> 00:23:08.510
to define the terms of the contest.

178
00:23:09.250 --> 00:23:10.310
You want to win?

179
00:23:13.850 --> 00:23:16.150
Change the terms.

180
00:23:17.830 --> 00:23:21.560
Improvise. adapt. cheat.

181
00:23:21.660 --> 00:23:24.430
Lean into your strengths.

182
00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:26.190
not his.

183
00:23:30.910 --> 00:23:32.270
Fight like a girl.

184
00:23:37.280 --> 00:23:38.410
Begin.

185
00:24:15.250 --> 00:24:16.380
Good.

186
00:24:39.170 --> 00:24:40.160
Where is she?

187
00:24:42.240 --> 00:24:44.940
Tatiana's things are gone.

188
00:24:42.240 --> 00:24:44.940
Did something happen to her?

189
00:24:48.950 --> 00:24:49.940
Sit.

190
00:24:56.420 --> 00:24:59.590
Tatiana did not have

191
00:24:56.420 --> 00:24:59.590
the qualities required

192
00:24:59.660 --> 00:25:01.490
to continue with the Ruska Roma.

193
00:25:03.500 --> 00:25:04.860
What are you talking about?

194
00:25:05.630 --> 00:25:07.830
She lacked the killer instinct

195
00:25:05.630 --> 00:25:07.830
I see in you.

196
00:25:08.670 --> 00:25:10.330
Your childhood was taken.

197
00:25:11.310 --> 00:25:13.330
This pain is what drives you.

198
00:25:14.510 --> 00:25:18.950
Tatiana... there is sadness. not pain.

199
00:25:19.010 --> 00:25:20.710
There's a difference.

200
00:25:21.720 --> 00:25:24.210
You two are now on different paths.

201
00:25:24.820 --> 00:25:26.480
Then why are you holding me back?

202
00:25:29.390 --> 00:25:30.380
I'm ready.

203
00:25:32.230 --> 00:25:33.390
Perhaps you are right.

204
00:25:38.500 --> 00:25:39.690
It is time.

205
00:25:46.870 --> 00:25:49.470
This is the final stage of your training.

206
00:26:12.700 --> 00:26:13.930
Oh. my God.

207
00:26:15.770 --> 00:26:17.360
Are you fucking kidding me?

208
00:26:18.410 --> 00:26:20.200
I'm a fucking test?

209
00:26:21.410 --> 00:26:23.400
How the mighty have fallen.

210
00:26:30.620 --> 00:26:32.050
Do you know who I am?

211
00:26:33.550 --> 00:26:34.540
No.

212
00:26:36.020 --> 00:26:37.010
I'm you...

213
00:26:38.260 --> 00:26:40.390
in ten fucking years.

214
00:27:54.370 --> 00:27:57.030
Somehow you managed to get out.

215
00:27:57.140 --> 00:27:59.540
but here you are back where you began.

216
00:28:02.310 --> 00:28:04.210
All of this for what?

217
00:28:22.800 --> 00:28:24.560
With this. Jardani.

218
00:28:24.670 --> 00:28:26.290
your ticket is torn.

219
00:28:33.970 --> 00:28:35.910
You can never come home again.

220
00:28:37.810 --> 00:28:39.540
Take him to the lifeboat.

221
00:28:41.580 --> 00:28:42.980
<i>Do svidanya.</i>

222
00:28:46.350 --> 00:28:48.020
<i>Do svidanya.</i>

223
00:28:56.560 --> 00:28:57.590
You're him.

224
00:28:58.870 --> 00:29:00.860
The one they call the Baba Yaga.

225
00:29:09.340 --> 00:29:11.400
The students all talk about you.

226
00:29:15.950 --> 00:29:17.210
How do I get outta here?

227
00:29:19.390 --> 00:29:21.450
The front door is unlocked.

228
00:29:22.890 --> 00:29:24.450
No. I mean...

229
00:29:24.560 --> 00:29:27.550
how do I start doing what you do?

230
00:29:30.560 --> 00:29:32.290
Looks like you already have.

231
00:29:33.530 --> 00:29:36.230
That door will lock sooner than you think.

232
00:29:36.870 --> 00:29:38.270
You can still leave.

233
00:29:39.310 --> 00:29:41.140
You still have a choice.

234
00:29:45.110 --> 00:29:46.600
Why didn't you leave?

235
00:29:49.580 --> 00:29:50.880
I'm working on it.

236
00:29:57.060 --> 00:30:00.620
The Director feels you are ready

237
00:29:57.060 --> 00:30:00.620
for your first contract.

238
00:30:02.600 --> 00:30:04.590
You will protect this woman.

239
00:30:05.400 --> 00:30:06.420
Katla Park.

240
00:30:06.500 --> 00:30:09.470
Her father is our primary charge.

241
00:30:09.570 --> 00:30:12.000
He is concerned that his competitors

242
00:30:12.110 --> 00:30:15.670
may try to get to him

243
00:30:12.110 --> 00:30:15.670
by ransoming his daughter.

244
00:30:15.780 --> 00:30:18.840
Your job is to make sure

245
00:30:15.780 --> 00:30:18.840
they don't get the chance.

246
00:30:19.580 --> 00:30:20.910
To infiltrate past security.

247
00:30:20.980 --> 00:30:25.650
you'll be using a modified

248
00:30:20.980 --> 00:30:25.650
3D printed Glock 43X

249
00:30:25.750 --> 00:30:29.950
with reinforced carbon fiber barrel.

250
00:30:25.750 --> 00:30:29.950
and polymer rounds.

251
00:30:34.030 --> 00:30:35.520
Rubber bullets?

252
00:30:35.630 --> 00:30:36.930
Problem?

253
00:30:39.530 --> 00:30:43.270
- No.

254
00:30:39.530 --> 00:30:43.270
- You'll find Miss Park at Minus Eleven.

255
00:31:59.610 --> 00:32:00.740
In position.

256
00:32:01.350 --> 00:32:02.370
Copy.

257
00:32:03.280 --> 00:32:04.950
I have the principal in sight.

258
00:32:06.890 --> 00:32:08.910
Hold your position.

259
00:32:10.460 --> 00:32:11.450
She can dance.

260
00:32:22.540 --> 00:32:24.970
I got movement at ten o'clock.

261
00:32:26.440 --> 00:32:27.570
A threat?

262
00:32:28.980 --> 00:32:30.140
Stand by.

263
00:32:36.920 --> 00:32:38.280
Hey!

264
00:32:38.390 --> 00:32:39.820
Definitely a threat.

265
00:32:59.240 --> 00:33:01.330
You should get out of the way.

266
00:33:01.440 --> 00:33:02.570
I can't.

267
00:33:04.810 --> 00:33:06.910
I understand.

268
00:35:02.930 --> 00:35:03.920
Hey!

269
00:36:40.530 --> 00:36:43.790
No. no. no.

270
00:36:40.530 --> 00:36:43.790
I don't want anyone to touch me right now.

271
00:36:43.860 --> 00:36:45.460
Hey. hey. It's okay.

272
00:36:46.570 --> 00:36:48.000
You're safe now. it's fine.

273
00:36:48.900 --> 00:36:50.060
Let's get you out of here.

274
00:38:48.150 --> 00:38:50.450
Hey. what the hell

275
00:38:48.150 --> 00:38:50.450
<i>is goin' on up there?</i>

276
00:38:50.520 --> 00:38:51.750
<i>Somebody respond.</i>

277
00:39:18.480 --> 00:39:19.880
Were you stuck in the elevator?

278
00:39:21.520 --> 00:39:23.620
Yes. It was very scary.

279
00:41:50.800 --> 00:41:53.830
Miss. something's leaking from your bag.

280
00:41:57.310 --> 00:41:58.470
Yes. Thank you.

281
00:41:58.540 --> 00:41:59.640
No problem.

282
00:42:06.790 --> 00:42:09.720
Is there a reason

283
00:42:06.790 --> 00:42:09.720
you've brought me a severed hand?

284
00:42:09.820 --> 00:42:11.220
Look at the scar.

285
00:42:14.030 --> 00:42:15.830
I've seen this before.

286
00:42:16.400 --> 00:42:19.230
That's the same scar

287
00:42:16.400 --> 00:42:19.230
as the man who murdered my father.

288
00:42:19.330 --> 00:42:21.460
It was a mark from a tribe.

289
00:42:22.040 --> 00:42:23.500
You knew who they were.

290
00:42:23.570 --> 00:42:24.830
How dare you?

291
00:42:25.470 --> 00:42:27.170
I have been protecting you.

292
00:42:27.240 --> 00:42:29.640
Why didn't you tell me who they were?

293
00:42:30.210 --> 00:42:32.640
